pam-truenas (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add SCRAM-PLUS channel binding (RFC 5929 tls-server-end-point) to
    pam_sm_authenticate, detecting a TLS-terminating MITM that relays an
    otherwise-valid client proof:
    - By default the precomputed binding is read from the uid=0 persistent
      keyring (published by middlewared from the active TLS certificate); pam_truenas
      parses no certificate at authentication time. scram_plus_cert=<path>
      overrides the source to read and hash a PEM file instead.
    - channel_binding=negotiate|require selects the policy: negotiate (default)
      enforces the binding for clients that use it and allows those that do not;
      require rejects clients that do not bind (failing closed when no binding
      is available).
  * Require libtruenas-scram (>= 0.2.0) for the new verification and binding
    computation symbols.

 -- Andrew Walker <andrew.walker@truenas.com>  Fri, 12 Jun 2026 01:06:38 +0000

pam-truenas (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release
  * SCRAM-SHA-512 authentication support
  * Session management with kernel keyring
  * Faillog/tally for brute-force protection
  * Session limit enforcement
  * Password fallback support

 -- Andrew Walker <andrew.walker@truenas.com>  Thu, 09 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000
